      "where": "Bibliography"
    }
  ],
  "technical_issues": [
    {
      "where": "Launch",
      "issue": "Kourou is approximately 5.2° N, not 45.05° N. The latitude comparison and launch-window reasoning therefore rely on an incorrect site coordinate."
    },
    {
      "where": "Launch",
      "issue": "The report proposes a 2025 launch using Vega E, while also stating its first launch will occur in 2024. Vega E was not an established available launcher for the proposed schedule; the launch choice and schedule require verification and contingency planning."
    },
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "At 600 km altitude, a circular sun-synchronous orbit requires a retrograde inclination near 97.8°. The reported 87.7924° is not sun-synchronous and conflicts with the claim of a retrograde orbit."
    },
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "RAAN does not indicate the launch facility's location; it specifies the inertial direction of the ascending node at a stated epoch. The orbital elements omit an epoch and use argument of latitude without specifying the reference frame or epoch."
    },
    {
      "where": "Orbit",
      "issue": "A 600 km orbit does not by itself establish adequate imaging resolution or swath coverage. No instrument resolution, swath, pointing, spectral requirements or coverage analysis is provided to substantiate reef-monitoring performance."
    },
    {
      "where": "Ground Control & Communications",
      "issue": "The reported access durations depend on the modeled ground-station coordinates, antenna masks and link assumptions, none of which are supplied. Pass access alone does not establish communications capacity or data downlink sufficiency."
    },
    {
      "where": "Mission Duration & EOL",
      "issue": "A drag sail is proposed but its area, deployment reliability, post-mission orbit lifetime and compliance with disposal guidance are not quantified. A passive sail does not guarantee prompt re-entry from 600 km."
    },
    {
      "where": "Bibliography",
      "issue": "The report cites Wikipedia, which is explicitly unacceptable under the task instructions; several references are incomplete bibliographic entries."
    }
  ],
  "overall": "A coherent Australian reef-monitoring concept is presented with substantial mission-segment coverage and STK access outputs. Important orbital and launch-site errors undermine the design’s central claims, while users, disposal performance and supporting files are insufficiently documented. Citation and editing weaknesses also limit report quality."
}
